WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.405 --> 00:00:15.275
"I don't want to be evaporated!"

2
00:00:15.635 --> 00:00:16.236
Ally cried.

3
00:00:16.256 --> 00:00:18.217
"I'll miss my friends.

4
00:00:18.678 --> 00:00:19.418
And my job.

5
00:00:20.059 --> 00:00:23.602
And I'll never see my parents ever again!"

6
00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:26.985
"Your reaction is illogical," Alpha said.

7
00:00:27.005 --> 00:00:30.468
"No, it's not," Ally said.

8
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.742
"Recall your life-form studies from fourth grade," Alpha said.

9
00:00:34.762 --> 00:00:37.724
"Remember what you were taught about Jorgandians?"

10
00:00:37.744 --> 00:00:41.386
"Um." Ally paused.

11
00:00:45.828 --> 00:00:47.729
think I was absent that day."

12
00:00:47.749 --> 00:00:50.551
"Negative!" Alpha snapped.

13
00:00:51.411 --> 00:00:53.792
"My records indicate you were present for that lesson."

14
00:00:53.812 --> 00:00:57.934
"Fine!" Ally sighed.

15
00:00:57.954 --> 00:01:00.356
"I guess I wasn't paying attention.

16
00:01:01.292 --> 00:01:04.593
Can you please just tell me what I need to know about Jorgandians?"

17
00:01:05.713 --> 00:01:12.495
"In the galactic year 874303, the Jorgandians vowed to destroy Astralia," Alpha said.

18
00:01:12.515 --> 00:01:19.177
"They despise the Astralians' peaceful way because it interferes with their goal of taking over the galaxy.

19
00:01:20.537 --> 00:01:27.819
Recently they developed a dangerous weapon—a small disk capable of instantly evaporating an Astralian life-form."

20
00:01:29.139 --> 00:01:31.100
"Jorgandians sound awful!"

21
00:01:31.592 --> 00:01:32.292
Mateo said.

22
00:01:32.312 --> 00:01:34.173
"What else, Alpha?"

23
00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:37.054
"They can move extremely fast.

24
00:01:37.894 --> 00:01:41.455
They are sly and wear a device much like your meld medallion.

25
00:01:42.175 --> 00:01:45.496
But their device enables them to take over other life-forms."

26
00:01:46.756 --> 00:01:48.037
"What does that mean?"

27
00:01:48.397 --> 00:01:49.217
Mateo asked.

28
00:01:50.377 --> 00:01:54.318
"It means, they can inhabit another life-form's body."

29
00:01:57.039 --> 00:02:00.260
Ally had to sit down; her legs were shaking so badly.

30
00:02:01.044 --> 00:02:02.565
"Correct," Alpha said.

31
00:02:02.585 --> 00:02:09.467
"The inhabited life-form looks and sounds much like its normal self, but the Jorgandian controls its every move."

32
00:02:09.487 --> 00:02:14.890
"So Mateo dropped down next to Ally, looking worried.

33
00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:18.911
"We won't be able to tell the Jorgandian from a real human?"

34
00:02:18.931 --> 00:02:22.233
"Correc—" Alpha's screen blinked off.

35
00:02:22.813 --> 00:02:24.654
Seconds later she started up again.

36
00:02:24.674 --> 00:02:28.415
"Oh no, Alpha, you're still glitching."

37
00:02:29.055 --> 00:02:30.236
Ally felt like crying.

38
00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:34.641
"We'll never be able to find the Jorgandian before it finds me!"

39
00:02:34.661 --> 00:02:37.542
"Incorrect," Alpha said.

40
00:02:37.562 --> 00:02:43.783
"While my systems are unstable in this primitive device, you can use your Astralian abilities to locate the

41
00:02:43.803 --> 00:02:46.144
Jorgandian." Mateo nodded.

42
00:02:46.164 --> 00:02:49.165
"All we have to do is walk around town, Ally!

43
00:02:49.685 --> 00:02:51.706
You can read the minds of everyone we pass.

44
00:02:52.426 --> 00:02:54.446
We'll find the Jorgandian in no time."

45
00:02:54.466 --> 00:02:58.287
"No, we won't," Ally said.

46
00:02:58.307 --> 00:03:02.212
"If it spots me first, I'll be evaporated."

47
00:03:03.353 --> 00:03:05.133
She jumped up and started pacing.

48
00:03:05.153 --> 00:03:10.275
"We have to figure out where the life-form is before I can leave the house again."

49
00:03:11.435 --> 00:03:13.195
Alpha displayed a map of Sandville.

50
00:03:13.215 --> 00:03:15.636
"The life-form is within this area.

51
00:03:16.516 --> 00:03:19.437
But I haven't been able to pinpoint its precise location."

52
00:03:20.597 --> 00:03:23.398
"That's a pretty big area," Mateo said.

53
00:03:23.418 --> 00:03:26.739
"It goes from Pepe's all the way to the copy shop."

54
00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.480
"Wait!" Ally halted.

55
00:03:30.452 --> 00:03:31.493
"It's Melanie!"

56
00:03:32.654 --> 00:03:33.474
Mateo frowned.

57
00:03:34.095 --> 00:03:35.155
"Why do you think that?"

58
00:03:35.175 --> 00:03:40.159
"Because she made me a Galorpian astroshake," Ally said.

59
00:03:40.179 --> 00:03:44.922
"And she said she had a necklace that was similar to my meld medallion."

60
00:03:44.942 --> 00:03:48.144
"I don't know.

61
00:03:48.824 --> 00:03:52.327
Melanie seems harmless, and Papi says she's a good worker.

62
00:03:53.287 --> 00:03:56.589
Maybe those things are just coincidences," Mateo said.

63
00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:59.051
"What do you think, Alpha?"

64
00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:00.132
Ally asked.

65
00:04:01.192 --> 00:04:04.595
"Jorgandians do love Galorpian food," Alpha said.

66
00:04:04.615 --> 00:04:09.039
"How am I supposed to work beside a Jorgandian?"

67
00:04:09.779 --> 00:04:10.880
Ally wrung her hands.

68
00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.222
"I'm in so much danger!

69
00:04:14.483 --> 00:04:16.965
Why didn't I pay better attention in school?"

70
00:04:18.006 --> 00:04:18.727
Alpha snorted.

71
00:04:18.747 --> 00:04:27.054
"If you had listened, Allyzooba, you would have remembered something important: Jorgandians have a powerful evaporation weapon.

72
00:04:27.935 --> 00:04:31.369
But they will not use it on you as long as humans are around.

73
00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:35.352
They fear humans would get alarmed, and possibly violent."

74
00:04:36.293 --> 00:04:37.894
"Phew!" Ally said.

75
00:04:37.914 --> 00:04:41.476
"I'll be safe as long as humans are around.

76
00:04:42.437 --> 00:04:45.199
But I can't avoid being alone with Melanie forever.

77
00:04:45.219 --> 00:04:50.383
I need a plan for throwing her off my trail, and I need one fast!"

78
00:04:50.403 --> 00:04:55.166
"What do Astralians do when they meet Jorgandians in space?"

79
00:04:55.626 --> 00:04:56.387
Mateo asked.

80
00:04:56.407 --> 00:04:57.908
"How do you fight them?"

81
00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.782
"We don't fight anyone, ever," Ally said.

82
00:05:01.802 --> 00:05:07.886
"Astralian cloaking devices protect our ships and planet from attack.

83
00:05:10.128 --> 00:05:14.411
If I still had my pod, I could stay in there, but She sighed.

84
00:05:15.311 --> 00:05:17.433
"That's long gone."

85
00:05:21.115 --> 00:05:21.976
have an idea!"

86
00:05:22.496 --> 00:05:23.357
Mateo brightened.

87
00:05:23.377 --> 00:05:25.038
"You can ask Dr.

88
00:05:25.098 --> 00:05:27.400
Lloyd for help in finding the Jorgandian.

89
00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:34.242
His alien beacon doesn't work, but maybe he's working on a new experiment to attract aliens."

90
00:05:35.463 --> 00:05:36.183
"Dr. Lloyd?"

91
00:05:36.783 --> 00:05:37.664
Ally shook her head.

92
00:05:37.684 --> 00:05:39.064
"No way!

93
00:05:40.245 --> 00:05:44.166
If he can detect a Jorgandian in town, then he'll detect me too!"

94
00:05:44.186 --> 00:05:47.087
"Allyzooba is correct," Alpha said.

95
00:05:47.107 --> 00:05:50.549
"It's up to us," Ally said.

96
00:05:51.369 --> 00:05:54.991
Ally wanted to come up with a plan, but she suddenly felt very tired.

97
00:05:56.531 --> 00:05:58.332
She sank onto her bed, yawning.

98
00:05:59.628 --> 00:06:01.771
"You must be exhausted from your trip.

99
00:06:02.692 --> 00:06:06.397
Get some rest; it will help you think more clearly," Mateo said.

100
00:06:06.417 --> 00:06:08.259
"Good idea."

101
00:06:11.243 --> 00:06:12.144
Ally yawned again.

102
00:06:12.164 --> 00:06:14.427
"See you in the morning."
